  "summary": "The health-tech landscape is being shaped by significant capital movements and emerging governance challenges. TRrexBio's $116 million IPO, Forbion's €2.3 billion fundraising, and multiple other funding rounds—including Vitalize's $31 million for hospital labor management and Tiny Health's $33 million for microbiome testing—signal continued investor confidence in biotech and digital health solutions. Meanwhile, regulatory and operational pressures are intensifying, with the FTC sending warning letters to 24 healthcare organizations over price transparency failures, the AMA flagging rising PBM market concentration, and cybersecurity experts warning hospitals to move beyond traditional disaster-recovery planning. AI governance and implementation remain critical focal points, as health systems grapple with deploying cognitive decline detection tools and ambient AI scribes while healthcare privacy leaders increasingly turn to AI for breach monitoring and data protection. Separately, policy shifts are underway, including the Trump administration's $90 Medicare Part B premium assistance announcement and renewed scrutiny of ACA fraud, while structural concerns persist around misaligned healthcare incentives, PBM opacity, and unmet needs in maternal health and social determinants of health.",
